# Documentation & Product Management

## Repository docs layout
```
docs/
  prd/        PRD-<nnn>-<slug>.md      product requirements per feature/epic
  erd/        ERD.md (+ mermaid diagram) data model, kept current
  adr/        ADR-<nnnn>-<slug>.md     architecture decisions (immutable once accepted; supersede, don't edit)
  runbooks/   deploy.md, rollback.md, incident.md, on-call per system
  postmortems/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md
  handoff/    client-facing operation & maintenance guide
  design/     DESIGN-BRIEF.md (reference sites, Stitch project/screen ids)
  brand/      BRAND-GUIDE.md
  testing/    TEST-PLAN.md
  marketing/  keyword-map.csv, CONTENT-PLAN.md, PAID-ADS-APPENDIX.md, experiments.md
  product/    POC.md, MVP.md
  business/   BUSINESS-MODEL.md, FORECAST.md, INVESTOR-DECK.md, reports/
README.md     what it is, how to run locally, env vars, scripts, links to docs
CHANGELOG.md  Keep a Changelog format, updated in every promotion PR
```

## PRD minimum
Problem, users/personas, goals & success metrics, scope / out of scope, user stories with acceptance
criteria (Given/When/Then), UX notes/links (Figma), data & integrations, non-functional requirements
(performance, security, privacy, RTL), risks, open questions, status.

## ERD
- Mermaid `erDiagram` in `docs/erd/ERD.md`, one table section per entity: columns, types, constraints, indexes, PII flag, tenant-owned yes/no.
- Updated in the same PR as the migration.

## ADR
Context → Decision → Alternatives considered → Consequences. Numbered sequentially. ADR-0001 records the
stack and hosting choice for the project.

## Tickets
- Each ticket: user story or bug report, acceptance criteria, estimate, labels (`feature`, `bug`,
  `tech-debt`, `security`, `client-request`), environment found in.
- Bugs: steps to reproduce, expected vs actual, env, logs/screenshots, severity (S1–S4).

## Maintenance (שוטף)
- Monthly: dependency updates, security advisories, backup restore test (staging), cost review, error-tracker triage.
- Quarterly: access review (who has prod/Meta/AWS access), secret rotation where needed, Meta Graph API version check.
- Every incident gets a blameless postmortem within 3 business days.
